                = succeed "\u201D" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unbiased"} unbiased
            %li
              %p
                An affine space over the field
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                is a vector space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A'
                together with a surjective linear map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi:A'\to k
                (the “slice of
                = succeed "\u201D" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Vect
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi π
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^{-1}(1)
          %p
            Clearly every vector space has an underlying affine space (and every linear map is affine linear), giving a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo →
                    %mi Aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U:Vect \to Aff
            = succeed "." do
              %em displacements
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heap"} heap
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo :
                  %mi Aff
                  %mo →
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D:Aff\to Vect
            in the other direction. One can verify that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(U(V))\cong V
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(D(A))\cong A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff
            would be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalent+categories"} equivalent categories
          %p
            The category of affine spaces is almost a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variety+of+algebras"} variety of algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            to be an affine space, although it does not have any particular vector space of displacements. (See
            %a{:href => "heap#empty"} heap#empty
            for discussion.)
          %p
            Note that there are a few different ways to think about the operations involved in the final three definitions (those not explicitly involving a vector space). The operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi x
                  %mo −
                  %mi y
                  %mo +
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu\colon x,y,z \mapsto x - y + z
            is the same as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mal%27cev+operation"} Mal'cev operation
            (i.e.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heap"} heap
            structure) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+group"} additive group
            of a vector space. It can be viewed as the point completing a parallelogram with given vertices
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            as the origin. The operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi x
                  %mo −
                  %mi r
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi r
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_*\colon r,x,y \mapsto x - r x + r y
            can be viewed as either a weighted average of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            (i.e. as
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi r
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1-r)x + r y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo −
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y-x
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            (i.e. as
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + r(y-x)
          %h3#details_and_comparisons Details and comparisons
          %p
            The first few definitions, which explicitly involve a vector space, make no especial use of the fact that the vector space is a vector space rather than merely an abelian
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsors"} torsors
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heaps"} heaps
          %h4#vectorvalued_differences Vector-valued differences
          %p
            In this definition, an affine space over a vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            together with a “subtraction” function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda\colon A\times A\to V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda\colon x,y \mapsto x-y
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda(x,x) = 0
              , or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo −
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x-x = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda(x,y) + \Lambda(y,z) = \Lambda(x,z)
              , or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo −
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo −
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo −
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x-y) + (y-z) = (x-z)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              For any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              there exists a unique
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda(y,x) = v
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo −
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y - x = v
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y - x = v
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y = x + v
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            by the third axiom. Hence we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x + v) - x = v
            and (by uniqueness)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + (y - x) = y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + 0 = x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi w
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo +
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x + v) + w = x + (v + w)
            by the first two axioms. Thus, these axioms suffice to make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            over the additive group of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            with the action
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +
          %p
            Note again that this would makes sense if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is any group, not just the additive group of a vector space.
          %h4#two_ternary_operations Two ternary operations
          %p
            This definition is an affine version of the usual definition of a vector space in terms of addition and scalar multiplication. However, in each case the affine operation needs to take an extra parameter. In reading the following axioms it helps to think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(x,y,z)
            as “the sum of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            relative to the basepoint
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_r(x,y)
            as “the product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\cdot y
            relative to the basepoint
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(x,x,y) = y
              (identity for addition)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(x,y,\mu(z,w,v)) = \mu(\mu(x,y,z),w,v)
              (associativity of addition)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(x,y,z) = \mu(z,y,x)
              (commutativity of addition)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_{r s}(x,y) = \Lambda_r(x, \Lambda_s(x,y))
              (associativity of scalar multiplication)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_1(x,y) = y
              (identity for scalar multiplication)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_0(x,y) = x
              (left zero for scalar multiplication)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo +
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_{r+s}(x,y) = \mu(\Lambda_r(x,y), x, \Lambda_s(x,y))
              (left distributivity of scalar multiplication)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_r(w, \mu(x,y,z)) = \mu(\Lambda_r(w,x), \Lambda_r(w,y), \Lambda_r(w,z))
              (right distributivity of scalar multiplication)
          .query
            %p
              %em> Joost
              \: Could it be that there is an axiom missing here ? One can go from Vector spaces to the 2 ternary operations definition and back, but I can’t see that by starting with the two ternary operations definition, going to vectorspaces and back, you get the same
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi Λ
                        %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(x,y,\Lambda_r(y,z))=\Lambda_r(x,\mu(x,y,z))
            %p
              %em> Toby
              \: Conceptually, there is something missing, which I've inserted as the left zero property of scalar multiplication. (The right zero property
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_r(x,x) = x
              follows from this using associativity of scalar multiplication with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s = 0
          %h4#one_quaternary_operation One quaternary operation
          %p
            This definition is an affine version of the less standard definition of a vector space in terms of a single operation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi r
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r,x,y\mapsto r\cdot x + y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            together with a single operation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi k
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu\colon k\times A\times A\times A\to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r,x,y,z)\mapsto \mu_r(x,y,z)
            and thought of as the sum “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\cdot x + z
            relative to the basepoint
            = succeed ",\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_1(x,y,y) = x
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_r(x,x,y) = y
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_1(x,y,z) = \mu_1(z,y,x)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_r(\mu_s(x,y,z),w,v) = \mu_{r s}(x,y,\mu_r(z,w,v))
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo +
                        %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{r+s}(x,y,z) = \mu_r(x,y,\mu_s(x,y,z))
          %h4#one_ternary_operation One ternary operation
          %p
            In the affine case (in contrast to the vector space case), it turns out that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            is invertible the “addition”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi x
                  %mo −
                  %mi y
                  %mo +
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y,z)\mapsto x-y+z
            can be recovered from the “scalar multiplication”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi r
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r,x,y)\mapsto r x + (1-r)y
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(x,y,z) = \Lambda_2(y,\Lambda_{1/2}(x,z))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            to be a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            together with a single operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi k
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda\colon k\times A\times A\to A
            such that the axioms for the two-ternary-operations definition are satisfied with this definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
          %p
            However, we can also simplify the requisite axioms in this presentation. The following axioms are easier to state if we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_r(x,y)
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi r
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1-r) x + r y
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi s
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r x + s y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo +
                  %mi s
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r+s=1
            for the expression to be defined.
          %ul
            %li
              Idempotence:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi s
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r x + s x = x
              whenever
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo +
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r+s=1
            %li
              Commutativity:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi s
                    %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mi s
                    %mi y
                    %mo +
                    %mi r
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r x + s y = s y + r x
              whenever
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo +
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r+s=1
            %li
              Associativity: whenever
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo +
                      %mi s
                      %mo +
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r+s+t=1
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi r
                              %mi x
                              %mo +
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %mi r
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mfrac
                                  %mi s
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo −
                                    %mi r
                                %mi y
                                %mo +
                                %mfrac
                                  %mi t
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo −
                                    %mi r
                                %mi z
                                %mo )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %mi s
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mfrac
                                  %mi r
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo −
                                    %mi s
                                %mi x
                                %mo +
                                %mfrac
                                  %mi t
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo −
                                    %mi s
                                %mi z
                                %mo )
                              %mo +
                              %mi s
                              %mi y
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mfrac
                                  %mi r
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo −
                                    %mi t
                                %mi x
                                %mo +
                                %mfrac
                                  %mi s
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo −
                                    %mi t
                                %mi y
                                %mo )
                              %mo +
                              %mi t
                              %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      r x + (1-r)\left(\frac{s}{1-r} y + \frac{t}{1-r} z\right)\\
                      (1-s)\left(\frac{r}{1-s} x + \frac{t}{1-s} z\right) + s y\\
                      (1-t)\left(\frac{r}{1-t} x + \frac{s}{1-t} y\right) + t z
                      }
              %p
                The first is defined whenever
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\neq 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\neq 1
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\neq 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                has characteristic
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neq 2
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r=s=t=1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo +
                      %mi s
                      %mo +
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r+s+t=1
                at the same time, so at least one of these expressions is always defined. We write
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi s
                      %mi y
                      %mo +
                      %mi t
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r x + s y + t z
                for the common value of whichever of them are defined.
            %li
              Cancellation: for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in k
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y\in A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi r
                      %mi y
                      %mo −
                      %mi r
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + r y - r y = x
          %h4#unbiased_definition Unbiased definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Th
                    %mi vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th_{vect}
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            of
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-tuples" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r_1,\dots,r_n)\in k^n
            representing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
            operation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_1,\dots,x_n)\mapsto r_1 x_1 +\dots+ r_n x_n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\ge 0
            and
            = succeed "-tuple" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r_1,\dots,r_n)
            of elements of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^n\to V
            (thought of as
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_1,\dots,v_n)\mapsto r_1 v_1+\dots r_n v_n
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Th
                    %mi aff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th_{aff}
            denote the subtheory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Th
                    %mi vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th_{vect}
            containing only those operations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r_1,\dots,r_n)
            such that
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_1+\dots+r_n=1
            %strong affine space
            is a nonempty model of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Th
                      %mi aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th_{aff}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_0x_0+\dots+r_n x_n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 0
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_0+\dots+r_n=1
            %strong affine (linear) combinations
            of elements of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            The axioms for the unbiased definition are most straightforward to see by writing out the operations of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Th
                      %mi aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th_{aff}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mn 00
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 00
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mn 00
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 00
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi n
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  r_0(s_{00} x_{00} + \dots + s_{0m_0} x_{0m_0}) + \dots + r_n (s_{n0} x_{n0} + \dots + s_{n m_n} x_{n m_n}) = r_0 s_{00} x_{00} + \dots + r_n s_{n m_n} x_{n m_n}.
          %p However, it also includes “permutation” axioms of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  r_0 x_0 + \dots + r_n x_n = r_{\sigma 0} x_{\sigma 0} + \dots + r_{\sigma n} x_{\sigma n}
          %p
            and also “duplication” and “omission” axioms. This Lawvere theory can be defined concisely as follows. The Lawvere theory of vector spaces is the opposite of the category of finite-dimensional vector spaces; its operations are all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combinations"} linear combinations
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+combinations"} convex combinations
            whose algebras are abstract
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"} convex space
            %em inhabited
            model.
          %p
            Given the unbiased definition in terms of a Lawvere theory, the previous three “biased” vector-space-free definitions can then be recovered by finding particular generating operations for the theory. In particular, this Lawvere theory is generated by
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi char
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} char(k)\neq 2
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi char
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} char(k)=2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r_0,\dots,r_n)\in k^{n+1}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\ge 3
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 0
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_0+\dots+r_n=1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_i
            are not all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_0\neq 1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  r_0 x_0 + \dots + r_n x_n = r_0 x_0 + (1-r_0)\left(\frac{1}{1-r_0} r_1 x_1 + \dots + \frac{1}{1-r_0}r_n x_n\right)
          %p
            so we have expressed the given
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_i=1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 0
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_0+\dots+r_n=1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x_0 + \dots + x_n = x_0 - x_1 + (2x_1 + x_2 + \dots + x_n)
          %p
            so we can still write this
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1=3
            (i.e.
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mi char
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=char(k)=2
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0 - x_1 + x_2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  r_0 x_0 + r_1 x_1 + r_2 x_2 = \big(r_0 x_0 + (1-r_0) x_2\big) - x_2 + \big(r_1 x_1 + (1-r_1) x_2\big).
          %h4#slice_of_
            Slice of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect
          %p (This gives definition 10.)
          %p
            Given an affine space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (with any other definition but number 10), the corresponding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
